MM the dense bf16 weight directly\\n                         (the compute floor; its load cost = raw_bytes / BW is\\n                         estimated from the reported ratio)\\n\\nReported per (codec, proj):\\n  * compress time, decompress time, compression ratio + compressed bytes\\nReported per (codec, layer, proj, N), under TWO conditions — isolated and with a\\nconcurrent H2D memcpy running (mimicking the next layer's weight offload):\\n  * raw GEMM, decomp+GEMM, fused latency P50/P95\\n\\nWhy the concurrent-H2D condition: decomp-then-GEMM writes the full dense weight\\nto HBM, which contends with the weight-offload H2D copy + HBM write bandwidth;\\nfused has no dense write and is contention-immune. An isolated sweep therefore\\nwrongly favours decomp for O/GateUp/Down — the in-engine flip the codec\\nthreshold tables (P4FlatCompressor._FUSED_MAX_N_TABLE etc.) already encode.\\n\\nTo characterise the fused KERNEL at every N (so production thresholds can be\\ncalibrated), the per-codec production N-thresholds are forced wide open.\\n\\nUsage:\\n  PYTHONPATH=$(pwd) ./.venv/bin/python benchmark_codec_decision.py\\n  ... --synthetic --check --n-values 1,64,256\\n  ... --csv codec_decision.csv\\n  ... --codecs zipserv,p4flat --projs o,gate_up\\n  ... --ats --codecs p4flat --projs gate_up   # GH200: exp->LPDDR/C2C, mant->HBM\\n\\nWith ``--ats`` (GH200 only) the codec's compressed-exponent stream is relocated\\nto Grace LPDDR (the raw sign|mantissa byte stream stays in HBM) and BOTH\\ncompressed strategies are re-measured reading that exponent over the NVLink-C2C\\nlink, adding two iso/h2d column groups:\\n\\n  * decmpATS  — decompress (exponent from LPDDR/C2C, mantissa from HBM) into a\\n                dense bf16 weight in HBM, then cuBLAS GEMM (still an HBM write).\\n  * fusedATS  — fused decode+GEMM; the exponent streams from LPDDR straight into\\n                the SMs, no dense-weight HBM staging at all.\\n\\nThis gives the direct HBM-vs-C2C comparison for the